{:org/id :org-global-refugee-block-committees
 :org/form-family :family-displaced-community
 :org/name "Refugee camp block committees and settlement leadership structures"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/category :cat-local-place
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-africa
 :org/countries ["BD" "KE" "UG" "JO" "TR" "SS"]
 :org/founding-date 1950
 :org/member-count 40000000
 :org/member-count-basis "llm-recall-unverified: displaced populations in camps and settlements are in the tens of millions (UNHCR reports total forced displacement above 100M, of which camp-based is a minority). The COMMITTEES themselves — majhi in Cox's Bazar, block and zone leaders elsewhere — are not counted anywhere."
 :org/legal-registration :unregistered
 :org/registration-note "Structurally unregistrable: members typically lack legal personality in the host state, which is exactly why this form belongs in this corpus."
 :org/governance-model :hierarchical
 :org/mission-statement "Block, zone and majhi structures that allocate aid, resolve disputes and represent residents to agencies — sometimes elected, sometimes appointed by the camp administration, always the operative government of the place."
 :org/coverage-note "Included deliberately: a corpus that only sees registered bodies cannot see people whose defining condition is having no standing."
 :org/data-provenance "llm-recall-unverified"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

